<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7083"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 6:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have solved part of his communications !  <BR>I know this isn&#39;t a huge part - But it is something. <BR> <BR>MO-ID-RUSE - Is the word-find. <BR> <BR>Look at the first block. The first line says &#34;MO&#34;.These are all of the MOs from the murders. <BR>Prowl - Fantasies - Follow- Victim - Details - Builds - Go for it &#40;There are more&#41; <BR> <BR>Now go down 13 lines <BR> <BR>Look at the second block. The first line says ID.These are all of his IDs.  <BR>Larry - Anderson - Telephone Co. - Gus - Officer &#40;more&#41;  <BR>Also all of the numbers fall in this block. This may be the most important thing if we can figure out their significance. <BR> <BR>Go down 13 lines <BR> <BR>Look at the third block. The first line says RUSE. These are the ruses he used.  <BR>Realtor - Insurance - Serviceman - For Sale - Help - Lost Dog. <BR> <BR>I know this is not a huge find, but a find nonetheless. And with BTK anything could be the one that brings him in. If these can match to the victim it may help the case.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve followed closely and have not seen this anywhere. If this has already been establish I shall hang my head in shame. LOL. <BR> <BR>iq <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
