<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7116"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:tbjostad@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Toto<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Toto<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey guys, great work, but before you go posting it everywhere, you need to this check out.   <BR> <BR>Go to the <b>GENERAL DISCUSSIONS</b> thread then <b>PUZZLES</b>.  Look for <b>Wichitaboy&#39;s 12/14/04</b> post.  He&#39;s got all the above &#40;and more&#41; plus links to pics of the puzzle as well.    <BR> <BR>Sorry IQ, great deductions though.  That&#39;s two great minds that have come to the same conclusion, think you guys hit the nail on the head!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7116-->
<!--Post: 7118--><!--Time: 1108191308-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7118"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Search this site &#34;grid&#34;. Very impressive, IQ &amp; Wichitaboy. My brain doesn&#39;t think that way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7118-->
<!--Post: 7131--><!--Time: 1108221023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7131"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In Wichitaboy&#39;s post, I didn&#39;t catch that the grid names MO, ID, RUSE were actually labeling the items beneath &amp; within its respective grid. <BR> <BR>&#40;Perhaps Wichitaboy was implying that, but I missed that particular aspect of it.&#41; <BR> <BR>IQ&#39;s post actually crystallized that for me. <BR> <BR>Great work -- both of you! <BR> <BR>Now, I guess we can connect each ruse to the murder?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
